Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.YEAR._2017  
  – "type": to isolate only “WatchEvent” rows.  
  – "repo":"name" (inside the VARIANT column "repo"): repository’s full name – used for grouping and for the join.  
  – "actor":"login" (inside the VARIANT column "actor"): GitHub user that produced the event – used for counting distinct watchers.  

• GITHUB_REPOS_DATE.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "repo_name": repository’s full name – join key to confirm the repo exists in the sample‑files table.  

Typical conditions we will need  
1. WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'            -- keep only watching events  
2. GROUP BY "repo_name"                    -- group at repo level  
3. HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor_login")>300 -- enforce > 300 distinct watchers  
4. ORDER BY "watcher_cnt" DESC             -- rank repos by watcher count  
5. LIMIT 2                                 -- top two  

Below are 10 exploratory‑to‑complex Snowflake SQL queries (all LIMITED to 20 rows) that gradually inspect and solve the problem.  
(Replace … with your warehouse / role / etc. as needed.)

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a handful of 2017 rows to understand overall structure.
SELECT 
  "id",
  "type",
  "repo",
  "actor"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show only WatchEvent rows to verify they exist and what their JSON looks like.
SELECT 
  "type",
  "repo",
  "actor"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Extract repo name from the VARIANT "repo" object for WatchEvent rows.
SELECT 
  "repo":"name"::STRING  AS "repo_name",
  "type"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Extract both repo name and actor login to verify distinct‐watcher logic.
SELECT 
  "repo":"name"::STRING  AS "repo_name",
  "actor":"login"::STRING AS "actor_login"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Count how many distinct watchers each repo received (no filter yet).
SELECT 
  "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same as #5 but now keep only repos with > 300 distinct watchers.
SELECT 
  "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING) > 300
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Order the >300‑watcher repos by watcher count (descending) to find leaders.
SELECT 
  "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
GROUP BY "repo_name"
HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING) > 300
ORDER BY "watcher_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Join the WatchEvent aggregation with SAMPLE_FILES to keep only repos 
--                 that actually appear in the sample_files table.
WITH watchers AS (
  SELECT 
    "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
    COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
  FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
  WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
  GROUP BY "repo_name"
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING) > 300
)
SELECT 
  w."repo_name",
  w."watcher_cnt"
FROM watchers w
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES" f
  ON w."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Same as #8 but remove duplicates that may come from SAMPLE_FILES 
--                 (one row per repo, use DISTINCT).
WITH watchers AS (
  SELECT 
    "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
    COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
  FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
  WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
  GROUP BY "repo_name"
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING) > 300
)
SELECT DISTINCT
  w."repo_name",
  w."watcher_cnt"
FROM watchers w
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES" f
  ON w."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
ORDER BY w."watcher_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – top two repositories with >300 distinct watchers in 2017 
--                  that also appear in SAMPLE_FILES.
WITH watchers AS (
  SELECT 
    "repo":"name"::STRING                      AS "repo_name",
    COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING)    AS "watcher_cnt"
  FROM "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."YEAR"."_2017"
  WHERE "type" = 'WatchEvent'
  GROUP BY "repo_name"
  HAVING COUNT(DISTINCT "actor":"login"::STRING) > 300
)
SELECT DISTINCT
  w."repo_name",
  w."watcher_cnt"
FROM watchers w
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS_DATE"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_FILES" f
  ON w."repo_name" = f."repo_name"
ORDER BY w."watcher_cnt" DESC
LIMIT 2;
```
